{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/821647-immortals-in-cwod","id":821647,"title":"Immortals in CWoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-02T08:48:13-08:00","id":821647,"title":"Immortals in CWoD","content":"I do not mean the Highlander style immortals. In the NWoD they had a book about immortals such as the Reborn, the Purified, the Eternals, Blood Bathers, etc.<br /> I was wondering if anyone thinks these types of immortals would be out of place in the CWoD. Mostly because I think vampires running into other immortals would be interesting. Also for the interpolitics of the Tremere realizing if they had looked a little harder they could have found ways to be immortal without the vampire weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11131-karst\u00e4rke","name":"Karst\u00e4rke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T09:17:25-08:00","id":821671,"title":"","content":"Mummies, both pre- and post- Mummy: the Resurrection, fill part of this slot for the CWoD, so there's some pre-existing space already there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T09:22:45-08:00","id":821675,"title":"","content":"I mean like someone like Dorian Grey being a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11131-karst\u00e4rke","name":"Karst\u00e4rke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T09:50:47-08:00","id":821692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karst\u00e4rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/821647-immortals-in-cwod#post821647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not mean the Highlander style immortals. In the NWoD they had a book about immortals such as the Reborn, the Purified, the Eternals, Blood Bathers, etc.<br /> I was wondering if anyone thinks these types of immortals would be out of place in the CWoD. Mostly because I think vampires running into other immortals would be interesting. Also for the interpolitics of the Tremere realizing if they had looked a little harder they could have found ways to be immortal without the vampire weaknesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>The WoD is a kitchensink setting... there is room for absolutley anything you'd find as curios and cool. There's quite a bit of room for characters like the ones in Immortals, and they're probaly rare enough that it's not particularly odd if the major splats don't really know much about them. Heck, most of them have only rudimentary knowledge of their own kind, letalone others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T11:01:55-08:00","id":821734,"title":"","content":"That is true, but I know some people are very adament about no NWoD in their OWoD and I was wondering if it made sense to try and suggest this?<br /> Honestly I think immortals and such could make for interesting villains in either Vampire or Werewolf. For Vampire, imagine a particularly annoying Vampire Hunter from the middle ages.. who is now stalking the streets with centuries of experience under his belt. Worse if he is creating a covenant of immortal Vampire Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11131-karst\u00e4rke","name":"Karst\u00e4rke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T16:56:06-08:00","id":821972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karst\u00e4rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/821647-immortals-in-cwod?p=821734#post821734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true, but I know some people are very adament about no NWoD in their OWoD and I was wondering if it made sense to try and suggest this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that line of thought is ridiculous myself. For the most part I prefer oWoD over nWoD but one thing I like about New is that it isn't as stagnant with it's setting. It has various groups interesting kinds of humans, beings beyond the core groups like the immortals and a number of other setting things that could be transplanted to the older setting to give it a bit more diversity with not just enemies but playable groups as well. It's got a lot of other content that I think could be added to Old Wold that would just make it better. Case in point, I think the stuff for thaumaturgy would work even better in an Ascension than it did in New World and better than Sorcerer did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T01:09:33-08:00","id":822189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/821647-immortals-in-cwod?p=821972#post821972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the most part I prefer oWoD over nWoD but one thing I like about New is that it isn't as stagnant with it's setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to point to that bit about stagnation. If your WoD is stagnant you're the only one responsible for that. The WoD lives and breathes according to your whim, and the books have changed a lot since the first editions when EVERYTHING had to be one of the splats. There is room for mystery, improvisation and liberal pillaging of groups, plots and concepts that are off the beaten Noun: The Verbing path.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T04:53:58-08:00","id":822273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karst\u00e4rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/821647-immortals-in-cwod#post821647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not mean the Highlander style immortals. In the NWoD they had a book about immortals such as the Reborn, the Purified, the Eternals, Blood Bathers, etc.<br /> I was wondering if anyone thinks these types of immortals would be out of place in the CWoD. Mostly because I think vampires running into other immortals would be interesting. Also for the interpolitics of the Tremere realizing if they had looked a little harder they could have found ways to be immortal without the vampire weaknesses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You want to make Tremere feel dumb have them meet a 2e Era meta plot Archmage. Practically immortal living in great wizard castles on mars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T05:02:08-08:00","id":822277,"title":"","content":"Never picked up Mage... is that really a thing in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11131-karst\u00e4rke","name":"Karst\u00e4rke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T05:09:26-08:00","id":822279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karst\u00e4rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/821647-immortals-in-cwod?p=822277#post822277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never picked up Mage... is that really a thing in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e too. They murdered almost all of them in Revised with a Umbral storm, though. That particular storm and what it did to the setting of Mage is still a contentious point among people who like Mage. In M20 the storm is entirely optional, so by default you still have insane places where godlike nigh-immortal Mages are still partying.<br /> <br /> Nota bene, they're not totally immortal - if they come back to real world for any length of time they will start having issues. So they mostly keep to their insane places .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T05:37:55-08:00","id":822293,"title":"","content":"I knew this game was weird lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11131-karst\u00e4rke","name":"Karst\u00e4rke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T06:08:58-08:00","id":822309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karst\u00e4rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/821647-immortals-in-cwod?p=822293#post822293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I knew this game was weird lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty cool actually. It just requires a very open mind to work. The Tremere thing is mostly an Ars Magica legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T06:22:11-08:00","id":822316,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I just like the idea of other immortals, other players on the chess board that Vampires and the like do not consider threats because aside from being immortal they are just humans (Purified not withstanding) but then being shocked when these immortal humans can do so much more than them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11131-karst\u00e4rke","name":"Karst\u00e4rke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T06:55:54-08:00","id":822342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karst\u00e4rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/821647-immortals-in-cwod?p=822316#post822316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I just like the idea of other immortals, other players on the chess board that Vampires and the like do not consider threats because aside from being immortal they are just humans (Purified not withstanding) but then being shocked when these immortal humans can do so much more than them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool. Go with it! Ananasi and old Mummies (before Mummy The Ressurrection) used to have totally that shtick. Anything specific you're planning to use?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:08:46-08:00","id":822398,"title":"","content":"An Eternal that is so old he had forgotten the time of his birth. His soul focus item is actually very old, its painting on a rock wall that he did when he was mortal. So its totally his, and now its considered prehistoric art and so its been protected, the cave he lived in is now guarded and so forth so he know its fairly safe and deep enough the pigments have held well.<br /> <br /> But during this time he has seen a ton, so much he has given up and found faith in humanity a number of times. But in the modern nights he is a recluse that has acquired a certain number of special magical and occult items that people might have need of. He is insanely wealthy due to his investments over the countless years and selling old items that where a dime a dozen back in the day. Like Ming Vases, he used to see them everywhere and now they are worth tons of money.<br /> <br /> A behind the scenes manipulator who has took long been removed from the front lines. Maybe he gets dragged into the fray to recover a stolen item or items. Maybe he was attacked and is now looking for the person behind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11131-karst\u00e4rke","name":"Karst\u00e4rke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:11:32-08:00","id":822447,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, could be interesting. Something like Vandal Savage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:47:02-08:00","id":822564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/821647-immortals-in-cwod?p=822189#post822189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd like to point to that bit about stagnation. If your WoD is stagnant you're the only one responsible for that. The WoD lives and breathes according to your whim, and the books have changed a lot since the first editions when EVERYTHING had to be one of the splats. There is room for mystery, improvisation and liberal pillaging of groups, plots and concepts that are off the beaten Noun: The Verbing path.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I need to further elaborate what I meant as far as stagnation goes. What you said does have truth to it in that it is up to the individual players to add or remove what they want from the setting yes. What I was referring to was that because of how tied down Old World is by it's own backstory and setting that depending on what you want to do you might have to change a large number of things. Even with it's added flexibility in later books it still very much has a &quot;this is how things are&quot; kind of feel to them. An example is that I add a lot of elements to the Ascension setting to actually make it feel like how it proclaims to be, especially in regards to other supernatural creatures and the Umbra that give it a level of diversity that it in many ways lacks. I'm not saying that it doesn't have its own complex setting but that same setting does often times come off as contradictory to the stated goal of the setting. That's just Ascension, I have stuff I can go on with any of the game line. Also I'm not saying that New World doesn't have its own flaws because it definitely does but one thing I love about it is that it gives a LOT of different material that it encourages to pick and choose from to customize the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T17:45:53-08:00","id":822915,"title":"","content":"Vandal savage is a good example. But you could play virtually anything. Heck highlander could be done with harvesters mixed with one of the others","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11131-karst\u00e4rke","name":"Karst\u00e4rke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T18:05:55-08:00","id":822926,"title":"","content":"A suggestion would be use resources like TVtropes to look up lists of immortal characters that you can get ideas from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T07:44:04-08:00","id":823339,"title":"","content":"The Immortality merit and Immunity to Death have both been in different books.<br /> <br /> I remember in Sir Gwain and the Green Knight the scene where he walked over and picked up his head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T13:30:07-08:00","id":823655,"title":"","content":"Which books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https